Log Normal distribution :(log(X) follows normal distribution)
-it is a continuous probability distribution with 
a distribution parameter mean and sd.

-As a SD is incraeses the PDF is having more tail.
Higher standard deviation means:
more spread
longer right tail
Distribution becomes more skewed.
-let X is any continuous random variable.
 X~lognormal(mean,SD) 
 then definately logX will follows a Gaussian distribution.
ex- dwell time=time user spends on website.
 many users → small time
few users → very large time
So it becomes right skewed → lognormal.

